mixin () {
  /// Static Markdown documentation of the backend's public API.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Racing Game Backend API\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis canister records finished runs of the vertical three-lane racing game and exposes them for read-back and analytics. It stores one `GameResult` per completed run: an auto-incrementing `id`, the achieved `score`, and the wall-clock `timestamp` at which the run was recorded.\n\n## Public methods\n\n### `recordRun(score : nat) : async nat`\n\nRecords one finished run for the calling principal and returns the assigned run id. The id is a monotonically increasing `nat` starting at `0` for the first recorded run. The timestamp is captured server-side at the moment the call executes; the caller cannot supply it.\n\n### `listRuns() : async [GameResult]`\n\nReturns every recorded run, newest first (descending by `id`). This is a query call: it is fast and unreplicated, and it never mutates state.\n\n### `getApiDoc() : async text`\n\nReturns this document. It is a static query and reads no state.\n\n### OQL methods (`schema`, `execute`)\n\nProvided by the OQL `Expose` mixin. `schema()` describes the `gameResult` entity; `execute()` runs a JSON query against it. The `gameResult` entity is registered `controllerOnly`, so only the platform controller (the Data Intelligence agent) can read it; end users cannot query it directly.\n\n## Authentication and authorization\n\n- `recordRun` is an update call. It accepts any caller, including anonymous ones, and does not gate on a role. It does not store the caller's principal, so recorded runs are not attributable to a user through this API.\n- `listRuns` is a public query call. Any caller, including anonymous ones, can read every recorded run.\n- The `gameResult` OQL entity is `controllerOnly`: only the canister controller can read it through `schema()` / `execute()`.\n- The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n- The shared authorization mixin (`MixinAuthorization`) is included and exposes its own role-management endpoints. `recordRun` and `listRuns` do not consult it.\n\n## Units and encoding\n\n- `score` is a non-negative `nat`; it is the raw in-game score, with no scaling or unit.\n- `timestamp` is an `int` in nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (UTC). Divide by 1,000,000 for milliseconds, or 1,000,000,000 for seconds.\n- `id` is a `nat` assigned by the canister; ids are unique and strictly increasing.\n- `GameResult` is a Candid record `{ id : nat; score : nat; timestamp : int }`.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- A run is recorded exactly once, when the frontend calls `recordRun` after the game ends.\n- `listRuns` is a query call and can be polled freely; it reflects the state committed by the most recent successful `recordRun`.\n- There is no server-side game session: the canister does not know a run is in progress and never transitions state on its own.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `recordRun` is **not idempotent**. Each successful call appends a new run and consumes a new id. Retrying after a timeout that actually succeeded creates a duplicate run. The frontend should call it once per finished game and not auto-retry.\n- `recordRun` has no destructive effects and never deletes or overwrites existing runs.\n\n## Errors, traps, and gotchas\n\n- `recordRun` traps only on an internal invariant failure (for example an id counter overflow); it does not reject callers.\n- `listRuns` returns an empty array when no runs have been recorded.\n- Because runs are not attributed to a principal, `listRuns` returns runs from every player of this canister, not just the caller's own.\n- The OQL `gameResult` entity is controller-only; a non-controller calling `execute()` receives an authorization error rather than an empty result.\n";
  };
};
